# uvxform

- Label: UV Transform
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 1 to 3
- Parameters: 27 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/uvxform.html
- Summary (EN): Moves, rotates and scales the values of a UV layer in 2D. Each UV value is treated as an XY location and replaced by the transformed result. Pixels are not moved.
- Résumé (FR) : Transforme les valeurs UV (translation, rotation, échelle) sans déplacer les pixels, avec une randomisation optionnelle par îlot grâce à l'entrée seed.

- Inputs meaning: ["uv: UV layer of image or texture coordinates to transform", "uvscale: Mono layer holding the original filter scale, combined with the transforms", "seed: ID layer supplying a random seed; pixels sharing an ID get the same random transform"]

- Key parameters: ["Pivot: local pivot for transformations", "Translate, Rotate (degrees), Uniform Scale, Scale (non-uniform): core transform controls", "Randomize group: Offset, Rotation, Uniform Scaling, Scale Min/Max, Uniform Scale Min/Max, Seed", "Fitting Method: None, Frame (uniform fit) or Stretch (non-uniform fit) to a rectangle set by Center and Size; per UV island when a seed input is connected"]

- Caveats: ["The node does not move pixels; it only changes the UV values each pixel represents"]

